@startuml 09-class-model
!include _style.iuml
title Core data model (starting point, not final)

hide empty methods

class ID <<value>> {
  client : uint32
  clock : uint32
}

class YataNode {
  id : ID
  left_origin : ID
  right_origin : ID
  parent : ID
  content : NodeContent
  deleted : bool  ' tombstone
}

abstract class NodeContent <<variant>>
class TextPayload {
  data : string
}
class MapPayload {
  keys : map<string, ID>
}
class ArrayPayload {
  head : ID
  tail : ID
}

class StateVector {
  clocks : map<client, clock>
}

class Branch {
  id : BranchId
  parent : BranchId
  fork_at : StateVector
}

class Author {
  jid : JID
  device : string
}

YataNode --> ID
YataNode *-- NodeContent
NodeContent <|-- TextPayload
NodeContent <|-- MapPayload
NodeContent <|-- ArrayPayload
Branch --> StateVector
ID ..> Author : client maps to\na JID + device (open)

note right of MapPayload
  "Immortal parents": an XML element
  holds a map of attributes and an
  array of children. Changing @fill
  updates the map; the element keeps
  its ID, so concurrent edits never orphan.
end note
@enduml
